                <pb facs="0749" n="735" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg735"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Davis, Acting
                        Secretary of State, to Mr. Pierrepont,
                        district attorney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1869-08-04"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi>
                        4, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush">Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwards
                        Pierrepont</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States District
                        Attorney, New York:</hi></p>
                <p>The Acting Secretary of the Navy, at the request of this Department, yesterday
                    ordered the commandant at New York to act under your directions in the matter of
                    the Spanish gun-boats. The Juniata, the Dale, the Dictator, the Frolic, and some
                    armed tugs are ready to co-operate with you.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. C. B. DAVIS.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
